# The demo project lives in its own repository:
#   https://github.com/PareshCybageWorks/demoproject_azurefabricmcp
#
# It is still cloned here side by side for local work, which is why it is
# ignored rather than absent. The framework must not carry project data --
# that separation is the point of the split.
01_demo-project/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Presentation material that is not framework code. Untracking alone does not
# stick -- a blanket `git add -A` re-adds it, which is how it landed twice.
#
# Scoped to the FILE, never the directory: AzureFabricMCP/ now holds the whole
# framework, and ignoring it wholesale would drop the framework from the repo
# on the next commit while everything still looked fine on disk.
/AzureFabricMCP/Quiz_AI_Master_Orchestrator.md

# Projects live in their own repositories; the framework holds no project data.
/02_demo-servicenow/
/03_live_demo/
